# Git Standards

## Conventional Commits

### Format obligatoire

```
<type>(<scope>): <description>

[body optionnel]

[footer optionnel]
```

### Types autorisés

| Type | Usage |
|------|-------|
| `feat` | Nouvelle fonctionnalité |
| `fix` | Correction de bug |
| `docs` | Documentation uniquement |
| `style` | Formatage (pas de changement de code) |
| `refactor` | Refactoring sans changement fonctionnel |
| `perf` | Amélioration de performance |
| `test` | Ajout ou modification de tests |
| `chore` | Maintenance, dépendances, CI |

### Exemples

```bash
# ✅ BON
feat(auth): add JWT token refresh mechanism
fix(api): handle null response from external service
refactor(users): extract validation logic to service
chore(deps): upgrade ansible to 2.15

# ❌ MAUVAIS
updated stuff
fix bug
WIP
```

### Breaking Changes

```bash
feat(api)!: change authentication endpoint response format

BREAKING CHANGE: response now returns user object instead of token string
```

### Règles commits

- Description en minuscules, sans point final
- Impératif présent ("add" pas "added")
- Max 72 caractères pour la première ligne
- Body pour expliquer le "pourquoi", pas le "quoi"

## GitFlow Workflow

### Branches principales

| Branche | Description |
|---------|-------------|
| `main` | Code production, jamais de commit direct |
| `develop` | Intégration, source des features |

### Branches de support

```
feature/123-user-auth    → branch from develop, merge to develop
release/v1.2.0           → branch from develop, merge to main + develop
hotfix/v1.2.1            → branch from main, merge to main + develop
```

### Commandes GitFlow

```bash
# Nouvelle feature
git checkout develop
git pull origin develop
git checkout -b feature/123-description

# Terminer feature
git checkout develop
git merge --no-ff feature/123-description
git branch -d feature/123-description

# Release
git checkout develop
git checkout -b release/v1.2.0
# ... bump version, fixes only
git checkout main && git merge --no-ff release/v1.2.0
git tag -a v1.2.0 -m "Release v1.2.0"
git checkout develop && git merge --no-ff release/v1.2.0

# Hotfix urgent
git checkout main
git checkout -b hotfix/v1.2.1
# ... fix critical bug
git checkout main && git merge --no-ff hotfix/v1.2.1
git tag -a v1.2.1 -m "Hotfix v1.2.1"
git checkout develop && git merge --no-ff hotfix/v1.2.1
```

## Semantic Versioning

```
MAJOR.MINOR.PATCH (ex: 2.1.3)

MAJOR → Breaking changes (API incompatible)
MINOR → Nouvelles features (rétrocompatible)
PATCH → Bug fixes (rétrocompatible)
```

## Pull Request Rules

1. Toujours via PR (jamais de push direct sur main/develop)
2. Minimum 1 approbation requise
3. CI/CD doit passer
4. Branche à jour avant merge
5. Supprimer branche après merge

## Checklist Git

- [ ] Commit message au format Conventional Commits
- [ ] Branche nommée selon GitFlow
- [ ] Version bump si release/hotfix
- [ ] Tag créé après merge sur main
- [ ] Branche supprimée après merge
